00:42:21.995 --> 00:42:24.395
Army Corps of Engineers best management

00:42:24.795 --> 00:42:26.315
practices were read from.

00:42:28.660 --> 00:42:31.460
Now it is an independent jurisdiction from

00:42:31.700 --> 00:42:37.060
the Andover Commission, right? An independent jurisdiction that we are going through a permit process with separately.

00:42:39.060 --> 00:42:41.140
And it is true that if you read the publication

00:42:42.075 --> 00:42:44.395
from the New England District of the Army Corps,

00:42:44.955 --> 00:42:45.355
that

00:42:48.235 --> 00:42:50.715
spans are the preferred method for crossings.

00:42:51.115 --> 00:42:53.195
However, if you read a footnote,

00:42:53.275 --> 00:42:56.395
the first time the word spans appears, there's a footnote that says

00:42:57.140 --> 00:42:59.540
three sided and open bottom culverts

00:42:59.620 --> 00:43:01.700
are included in definition

00:43:02.740 --> 00:43:03.620
of span.

00:43:04.420 --> 00:43:08.660
So ours is a box culvert, and that again is a little bit different, right? We will have to

00:43:09.615 --> 00:43:12.975
restore the stream bed after we, you know, dig it and

00:43:13.295 --> 00:43:15.135
drop the box culvert in.

00:43:15.615 --> 00:43:19.535
However, I think it's really important for the commission to understand

00:43:19.775 --> 00:43:24.575
that it's not the army corps position. They are not saying that bridges are preferred,

00:43:25.590 --> 00:43:27.750
spans are preferred, not bridges.

00:43:28.390 --> 00:43:29.350
And we really,

00:43:29.670 --> 00:43:33.830
we, you know, it's confirmation of that. We've, we've talked to the, to the army corps.

00:43:34.150 --> 00:43:37.270
They're familiar with what we're doing. Nobody has even suggested

00:43:37.910 --> 00:43:41.755
at all that a bridge spanning the whole channel

00:43:42.475 --> 00:43:45.915
is, you know, is what we should be doing here instead of the crossing.

00:43:46.555 --> 00:43:49.915
They've informed us that the culvert is what we to

00:43:50.395 --> 00:43:52.075
do to comply with the practices.

